{"article_ids": ["b4c2f06bca4278c0"], "canonical_title": "How we found 24 Android vulnerabilities using our open source AI security agent", "category": "open_source", "confidence": 0.9, "description": "GitHub researchers used their open‑source AI‑powered security agent to scan Android applications, identifying 24 distinct vulnerabilities. The blog details the targeted AI taskflows, describes the critical bugs uncovered, and provides instructions for running the same agent on other apps.", "entities": [], "first_seen": "2026-09-28T19:00:00Z", "id": "evt_b4c2f06bca4278c0", "importance_score": 6.192, "last_updated": "2026-09-28T19:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["github-blog"]}
{"article_ids": ["1b03b5415061c07e"], "canonical_title": "CSI-Agent: LLM-Assisted Few-Shot Adaptation for Cross-Domain Wi-Fi CSI Sensing", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.7, "description": "The paper proposes CSI-Agent, a system that uses a large language model (LLM) to assist few‑shot adaptation of Wi‑Fi channel state information (CSI) sensing models when deployed across different users or environments. The approach aims to overcome the brittleness of existing CSI‑based activity recognition models by generating adaptation guidance from limited target‑domain data rather than relying on a single offline adaptation method.", "entities": ["term:csi"], "first_seen": "2026-09-29T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_1b03b5415061c07e", "importance_score": 6.14, "last_updated": "2026-09-29T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["b50a45e3b01b649b"], "canonical_title": "Quantization Thresholds Replicate, Failure Modes Do Not: A Three-Model Study of Agentic Tool Use in Polish from 8-bit to 2-bit", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "Researchers evaluated GGUF quantization effects on Polish-language agentic tool use by testing three models (Bielik-11B-v3.0, its pruned version, and distilled Bielik-Minitron-7B-v3.0) across 8‑bit to 2‑bit precisions. They introduced PolAgentBench, a deterministic benchmark with 67 main tasks (including 15 adversarial probes) and a 46‑task arithmetic isolation ladder. Results show that quantization thresholds are replicated across models, but new failure modes appear at lower bit widths.", "entities": ["term:gguf"], "first_seen": "2026-09-29T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_b50a45e3b01b649b", "importance_score": 6.14, "last_updated": "2026-09-29T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-cl"]}
{"article_ids": ["e5f4481e480a7cd4"], "canonical_title": "SenseAgent: An LLM Agent for Adaptive Cross-Domain IMU Sensing", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.78, "description": "The paper introduces SenseAgent, an LLM‑based agent that dynamically adapts inertial measurement unit (IMU) sensing models when they are applied to new users, devices, or body positions. Unlike prior static approaches that rely on pre‑training stronger representations, data augmentation, or a single chosen adaptation method before deployment, SenseAgent selects and configures adaptation strategies at runtime to handle cross‑domain shifts.", "entities": ["term:imu"], "first_seen": "2026-09-29T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_e5f4481e480a7cd4", "importance_score": 5.94, "last_updated": "2026-09-29T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
